IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa26-support`

-- coa26-ch3b.l4: Companies Act 2006, Part 42, Chapter 3 (Auditors General), ss 1232 to 1238: information (matters to be notified to
-- the Independent Supervisor and its power to call for information), suspension notices and their effect, compliance orders,
-- proceedings involving the Independent Supervisor, and grants. Lines 17457-17517 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: as in coa26-ch1.l4 (MAYBE BOOLEAN; JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words, each such branch
-- with a FALSE-kind comment; NOTHING otherwise, each branch with a NOTHING-kind comment). Months are counted with `Date`, which rolls a
-- day that does not exist in the later month forward: a month-end date is a fork (see the fork register).
-- The duties of ss 1235(1) and (2) are also regulative rules (traced); a DEONTIC outcome cannot be asserted on the stable binary.

§§ `Information`

§§§ `s 1232 Matters to be notified to the Independent Supervisor`

-- src:17459 | (1) The Independent Supervisor may require an Auditor General—
-- src:17460 | (a) to notify the Independent Supervisor immediately of the occurrence of such events as it may specify in writing and to give it such information in respect of those events as is so specified;
-- src:17461 | (b) to give the Independent Supervisor, at such times or in respect of such periods as it may specify in writing, such information as is so specified.
@ref s 1232(1) Power to require notification and information (src:17459-17461)
GIVEN `the person is an Auditor General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement is to notify the Independent Supervisor immediately of the occurrence of such events as the Independent Supervisor may specify in writing and to give the Independent Supervisor such information in respect of those events as is so specified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement is to give the Independent Supervisor, at such times or in respect of such periods as the Independent Supervisor may specify in writing, such information as is so specified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1232(1) the Independent Supervisor may require the body to notify or give information` MEANS
    -- the power reaches only the body named in the subsection and only the two kinds of requirement in paragraphs (a) and (b)
    IF `the person is an Auditor General` AND (`the requirement is to notify the Independent Supervisor immediately of the occurrence of such events as the Independent Supervisor may specify in writing and to give the Independent Supervisor such information in respect of those events as is so specified` OR `the requirement is to give the Independent Supervisor, at such times or in respect of such periods as the Independent Supervisor may specify in writing, such information as is so specified`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Independent Supervisor may require" the body named in subsection (1) to notify or give information as in paragraphs (a) and (b)

-- src:17462 | (2) The notices and information required to be given must be such as the Independent Supervisor may reasonably require for the exercise of the functions conferred on it by or by virtue of this Part.
@ref s 1232(2) The notices and information must be reasonably required (src:17462)
GIVEN `the notice or information required is such as the Independent Supervisor may reasonably require for the exercise of its functions under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1232(2) the notice or information required is within subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `the notice or information required is such as the Independent Supervisor may reasonably require for the exercise of its functions under this Part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notices and information required to be given must be such as the Independent Supervisor may reasonably require" (a bare "must" not done: decided case by case, see the fork register)

-- src:17463 | (3) The Independent Supervisor may require information given under this section to be given in a specified form or verified in a specified manner.
@ref s 1232(3) Form and verification (src:17463)
GIVEN `the information is information given under section 1232` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Independent Supervisor requires the information to be given in a specified form or verified in a specified manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1232(3) the Independent Supervisor may require the information to be given in a specified form or verified in a specified manner` MEANS
    IF `the information is information given under section 1232` AND `the Independent Supervisor requires the information to be given in a specified form or verified in a specified manner`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Independent Supervisor may require information given under this section to be given in a specified form or verified in a specified manner"

-- src:17464 | (4) Any notice or information required to be given under this section must be given in writing unless the Independent Supervisor specifies or approves some other manner.
@ref s 1232(4) The notice or information must be in writing (src:17464)
GIVEN `the notice or information is required to be given under section 1232` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Independent Supervisor specifies or approves some other manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1232(4) the notice or information must be given in writing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the notice or information is required to be given under section 1232` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any notice or information required to be given under this section"
        IF `the Independent Supervisor specifies or approves some other manner` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be given in writing unless the Independent Supervisor specifies or approves some other manner" (an "unless" once met: decided case by case, see the fork register)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE


§§§ `s 1233 The Independent Supervisor's power to call for information`

-- src:17466 | (1) The Independent Supervisor may by notice in writing require an Auditor General to give it such information as it may reasonably require for the exercise of the functions conferred on it by or by virtue of this Part.
@ref s 1233(1) Power to call for information by notice (src:17466)
GIVEN `the person is an Auditor General` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the requirement is made by notice in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is such as the Independent Supervisor may reasonably require for the exercise of its functions under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1233(1) the Independent Supervisor may by notice in writing require the person to give the information` MEANS
    IF `coa26 support the answer is JUST TRUE` `the person is an Auditor General` AND `the requirement is made by notice in writing` AND `the information is such as the Independent Supervisor may reasonably require for the exercise of its functions under this Part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Independent Supervisor may by notice in writing require" the persons named "such information as the Independent Supervisor may reasonably require"

-- src:17467 | (2) The Independent Supervisor may require that any information which it requires under this section is to be given within such reasonable time and verified in such manner as it may specify.
@ref s 1233(2) Time and verification (src:17467)
GIVEN `the Independent Supervisor requires the information within such reasonable time and verified in such manner as the Independent Supervisor specifies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time specified is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1233(2) the Independent Supervisor may require the information to be given within a reasonable time and verified in a specified manner` MEANS
    IF `the Independent Supervisor requires the information within such reasonable time and verified in such manner as the Independent Supervisor specifies` AND `the time specified is reasonable`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "within such reasonable time and verified in such manner as the Independent Supervisor may specify"


§§ `Enforcement`

§§§ `s 1234 Suspension notices`

-- src:17470 | (1) The Independent Supervisor may issue—
-- src:17471 | (a) a notice (a “suspension notice”) suspending an Auditor General's eligibility for appointment as a statutory auditor in relation to all persons, or any specified person or persons, indefinitely or until a date specified in the notice;
-- src:17472 | (b) a notice amending or revoking a suspension notice previously issued to an Auditor General.
@ref s 1234(1) The notices the Independent Supervisor may issue (src:17470-17472)
GIVEN `the notice suspends an Auditor General's eligibility for appointment as a statutory auditor in relation to all persons, or any specified person or persons, indefinitely or until a date specified in the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice amends or revokes a suspension notice previously issued to an Auditor General` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1234(1) the Independent Supervisor may issue the notice` MEANS
    IF `the notice suspends an Auditor General's eligibility for appointment as a statutory auditor in relation to all persons, or any specified person or persons, indefinitely or until a date specified in the notice` OR `the notice amends or revokes a suspension notice previously issued to an Auditor General`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Independent Supervisor may issue— (a) a notice (a “suspension notice”) suspending ... (b) a notice amending or revoking a suspension notice"

-- src:17473 | (2) In determining whether it is appropriate to issue a notice under subsection (1), the Independent Supervisor must have regard to—
-- src:17474 | (a) the Auditor General's performance of the obligations imposed on him by or by virtue of this Part, and
-- src:17475 | (b) the Auditor General's performance of his functions as a statutory auditor.
@ref s 1234(2) Matters to have regard to (src:17473-17475)
GIVEN `the Independent Supervisor had regard to the Auditor General's performance of the obligations imposed on him by or by virtue of Part 42` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Independent Supervisor had regard to the Auditor General's performance of his functions as a statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1234(2) the Independent Supervisor has had regard to the matters in subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `the Independent Supervisor had regard to the Auditor General's performance of the obligations imposed on him by or by virtue of Part 42` AND `the Independent Supervisor had regard to the Auditor General's performance of his functions as a statutory auditor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Independent Supervisor must have regard to— (a) ... and (b) ..." (a bare "must" not done: decided case by case, see the fork register)

-- src:17476 | (3) A notice under subsection (1) must—
-- src:17477 | (a) be in writing, and
-- src:17478 | (b) state the date on which it takes effect (which must be after the period of three months beginning with the date on which it is issued).
@ref s 1234(3) The form of the notice and the date it takes effect (src:17476-17478)
GIVEN `the notice is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the date on which it takes effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the notice is issued` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the notice takes effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1234(3) the notice meets subsection (3)` MEANS
    -- the date must be after the period of three months beginning with the date of issue: the same day three months on is the first day after it
    IF     `the notice is in writing`
       AND `the notice states the date on which it takes effect`
       AND `the date on which the notice takes effect` AT LEAST `three months on`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A notice under subsection (1) must— (a) be in writing, and (b) state the date on which it takes effect (which must be after the period of three months beginning with the date on which it is issued)."
    WHERE
        `three months on` MEANS
            Date (DATE_DAY `the date on which the notice is issued`) (DATE_MONTH `the date on which the notice is issued` PLUS 3) (DATE_YEAR `the date on which the notice is issued`)

-- src:17479 | (4) Before issuing a notice under subsection (1), the Independent Supervisor must—
-- src:17480 | (a) give written notice of its intention to do so to the Auditor General, and
-- src:17481 | (b) publish the notice mentioned in paragraph (a) in such manner as it thinks appropriate for bringing it to the attention of any other persons who are likely to be affected.
@ref s 1234(4) Notice of intention (src:17479-17481)
GIVEN `the Independent Supervisor gave written notice of its intention to issue the notice to the Auditor General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Independent Supervisor published the notice in such manner as it thinks appropriate for bringing it to the attention of any other persons who are likely to be affected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1234(4) the Independent Supervisor has complied with the duty before issuing the notice` MEANS
    IF `the Independent Supervisor gave written notice of its intention to issue the notice to the Auditor General` AND `the Independent Supervisor published the notice in such manner as it thinks appropriate for bringing it to the attention of any other persons who are likely to be affected`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Before issuing a notice under subsection (1), the Independent Supervisor must— (a) give written notice of its intention to do so to the Auditor General, and (b) publish the notice"

-- src:17482 | (5) A notice under subsection (4) must—
-- src:17483 | (a) state the reasons for which the Independent Supervisor proposes to act, and
-- src:17484 | (b) give particulars of the rights conferred by subsection (6).
@ref s 1234(5) Content of the notice of intention (src:17482-17484)
GIVEN `the notice under subsection (4) states the reasons for which the Independent Supervisor proposes to act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice under subsection (4) gives particulars of the rights conferred by subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1234(5) the notice of intention has the required content` MEANS
    IF `the notice under subsection (4) states the reasons for which the Independent Supervisor proposes to act` AND `the notice under subsection (4) gives particulars of the rights conferred by subsection (6)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A notice under subsection (4) must— (a) state the reasons for which the Independent Supervisor proposes to act, and (b) give particulars of the rights conferred by subsection (6)."

-- src:17486 | (7) The persons within this subsection are—
-- src:17487 | (a) the Auditor General, and
-- src:17488 | (b) any other person who appears to the Independent Supervisor to be affected.
@ref s 1234(7) The persons who may make representations (src:17486-17488)
GIVEN `the person is the Auditor General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is any other person who appears to the Independent Supervisor to be affected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1234(7) the person is within subsection (7)` MEANS
    IF `the person is the Auditor General` OR `the person is any other person who appears to the Independent Supervisor to be affected`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The persons within this subsection are— (a) the Auditor General, and (b) any other person who appears to the Independent Supervisor to be affected." (a list closed by "are", read as the keel reads "are": a lawyer's reading)

-- src:17485 | (6) A person within subsection (7) may, within the period of three months beginning with the date of service or publication of the notice under subsection (4) or such longer period as the Independent Supervisor may allow, make written representations to the Independent Supervisor and, if desired, oral representations to a person appointed for that purpose by the Independent Supervisor.
@ref s 1234(6) The right to make representations (src:17485)
GIVEN `the person is within subsection (7)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the date of service or publication of the notice under subsection (4)` IS A DATE
      `the day the representations are made` IS A DATE
      `the last day of any longer period the Independent Supervisor allows` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1234(6) the person may make written representations and, if desired, oral representations` MEANS
    -- "within the period of 3 months beginning with the date of service or publication ... or such longer period as the Independent Supervisor may allow"
    CONSIDER `the person is within subsection (7)`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person within subsection (7) may"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person appears to the Independent Supervisor to be affected is not known
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the day the representations are made` AT LEAST `the date of service or publication of the notice under subsection (4)` AND (`the day the representations are made` LESS THAN `three months on` OR `within the longer period`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, within the period of 3 months beginning with the date of service or publication of the notice under subsection (4) or such longer period as the Independent Supervisor may allow, make written representations" (a period fixed in the text's own words: ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))
    WHERE
        `three months on` MEANS
            Date (DATE_DAY `the date of service or publication of the notice under subsection (4)`) (DATE_MONTH `the date of service or publication of the notice under subsection (4)` PLUS 3) (DATE_YEAR `the date of service or publication of the notice under subsection (4)`)
        `within the longer period` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the last day of any longer period the Independent Supervisor allows`
            WHEN JUST lastDay THEN `the day the representations are made` AT MOST lastDay
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- src:17489 | (8) The Independent Supervisor must have regard to any representations made in accordance with subsection (6) in determining—
-- src:17490 | (a) whether to issue a notice under subsection (1), and
-- src:17491 | (b) the terms of any such notice.
@ref s 1234(8) Regard to representations (src:17489-17491)
GIVEN `representations were made in accordance with subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Independent Supervisor had regard to them in determining whether to issue a notice under subsection (1) and the terms of any such notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1234(8) the Independent Supervisor has complied with the duty to have regard to the representations` MEANS
    IF NOT `representations were made in accordance with subsection (6)`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any representations made in accordance with subsection (6)"
    ELSE IF `the Independent Supervisor had regard to them in determining whether to issue a notice under subsection (1) and the terms of any such notice`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Independent Supervisor must have regard to any representations made in accordance with subsection (6) in determining— (a) whether to issue a notice under subsection (1), and (b) the terms of any such notice."

-- src:17492 | (9) If in any case the Independent Supervisor considers it appropriate to do so in the public interest it may issue a notice under subsection (1), without regard to the restriction in subsection (3)(b), even if—
-- src:17493 | (a) no notice has been given or published under subsection (4), or
-- src:17494 | (b) the period of time for making representations in pursuance of such a notice has not expired.
@ref s 1234(9) Issuing the notice in the public interest (src:17492-17494)
GIVEN `the Independent Supervisor considers it appropriate to do so in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1234(9) the Independent Supervisor may issue the notice without regard to the restriction in subsection (3)(b)` MEANS
    IF `the Independent Supervisor considers it appropriate to do so in the public interest`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- even if no notice has been given or published under subsection (4), or the time for representations has not expired
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If in any case the Independent Supervisor considers it appropriate to do so in the public interest it may issue a notice under subsection (1), without regard to the restriction in subsection (3)(b)": a grant limited by its own "if", so the case outside the limit is not decided here (name-test sweep of 2026-11-12, F25)

-- src:17495 | (10) On issuing a notice under subsection (1), the Independent Supervisor must—
-- src:17496 | (a) give a copy of the notice to the Auditor General, and
-- src:17497 | (b) publish the notice in such manner as it thinks appropriate for bringing it to the attention of persons likely to be affected.
@ref s 1234(10) On issuing the notice (src:17495-17497)
GIVEN `the Independent Supervisor gave a copy of the notice to the Auditor General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Independent Supervisor published the notice in such manner as it thinks appropriate for bringing it to the attention of persons likely to be affected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1234(10) the Independent Supervisor has complied with the duty on issuing the notice` MEANS
    IF `the Independent Supervisor gave a copy of the notice to the Auditor General` AND `the Independent Supervisor published the notice in such manner as it thinks appropriate for bringing it to the attention of persons likely to be affected`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On issuing a notice under subsection (1), the Independent Supervisor must— (a) give a copy of the notice to the Auditor General, and (b) publish the notice"

-- src:17498 | (11) In this section “specified” means specified in, or of a description specified in, the suspension notice in question.
@ref s 1234(11) "specified" (src:17498)
GIVEN `the person is specified in, or is of a description specified in, the suspension notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1234(11) the person is specified` MEANS
    IF `the person is specified in, or is of a description specified in, the suspension notice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this section “specified” means specified in, or of a description specified in, the suspension notice in question."

§§§ `s 1235 Effect of suspension notices`

-- src:17500 | (1) An Auditor General must not act as a statutory auditor at any time when a suspension notice issued to him in respect of the audited person has effect.
@ref s 1235(1) An Auditor General must not act while a suspension notice has effect (src:17500)
GIVEN `a suspension notice issued to the Auditor General in respect of the audited person has effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1235(1) the Auditor General may act as statutory auditor of the audited person` MEANS
    IF `a suspension notice issued to the Auditor General in respect of the audited person has effect`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An Auditor General must not act as a statutory auditor at any time when a suspension notice issued to him in respect of the audited person has effect."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "at any time when": the subsection forbids acting only while the notice has effect and grants no permission

`s 1235(1) acts as statutory auditor of the audited person` MEANS `Action of a party` OF Auditor, Company, "acts as statutory auditor of the audited person"

-- src:17500 | (1) An Auditor General must not act as a statutory auditor at any time when a suspension notice issued to him in respect of the audited person has effect.
@ref s 1235(1) The prohibition, as a regulative rule (src:17500)
GIVEN `a suspension notice issued to the Auditor General in respect of the audited person has effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 1235(1) the prohibition on acting while a suspension notice has effect` MEANS
    IF `a suspension notice issued to the Auditor General in respect of the audited person has effect`
    THEN PARTY Auditor
         SHANT `s 1235(1) acts as statutory auditor of the audited person`
         LEST BREACH BY Auditor BECAUSE "acted as statutory auditor at a time when a suspension notice issued to the Auditor General in respect of the audited person had effect"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:17501 | (2) If at any time during an Auditor General's term of office as a statutory auditor a suspension notice issued to him in respect of the audited person takes effect, he must immediately—
-- src:17502 | (a) resign his office (with immediate effect), and
-- src:17503 | (b) give notice in writing to the audited person that he has resigned by reason of his becoming ineligible for appointment.
@ref s 1235(2) Duty to resign and give notice when the suspension notice takes effect (src:17501-17503)
GIVEN `the person is an Auditor General holding office as a statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a suspension notice issued to him in respect of the audited person takes effect at a time during his term of office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1235(2) the Auditor General must immediately resign and give notice` MEANS
    IF `the person is an Auditor General holding office as a statutory auditor` AND `a suspension notice issued to him in respect of the audited person takes effect at a time during his term of office`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If at any time during an Auditor General's term of office as a statutory auditor a suspension notice issued to him in respect of the audited person takes effect, he must immediately" (a duty whose "if" is unmet: decided case by case, see the fork register)

`s 1235(2)(a) resigns his office with immediate effect` MEANS `Action of a party` OF Auditor, Company, "resigns his office with immediate effect"
`s 1235(2)(b) gives notice in writing that he has resigned by reason of his becoming ineligible` MEANS `Action of a party` OF Auditor, Company, "gives notice in writing to the audited person that he has resigned by reason of his becoming ineligible for appointment"

-- src:17501 | (2) If at any time during an Auditor General's term of office as a statutory auditor a suspension notice issued to him in respect of the audited person takes effect, he must immediately—
-- src:17502 | (a) resign his office (with immediate effect), and
-- src:17503 | (b) give notice in writing to the audited person that he has resigned by reason of his becoming ineligible for appointment.
@ref s 1235(2) The duty, as a regulative rule (src:17501-17503)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 1235(2) the duty of an Auditor General when a suspension notice takes effect` MEANS
    PARTY Auditor
    MUST `s 1235(2)(a) resigns his office with immediate effect`
    WITHIN 0
    HENCE (
        PARTY Auditor
        MUST `s 1235(2)(b) gives notice in writing that he has resigned by reason of his becoming ineligible`
        WITHIN 0
        LEST BREACH BY Auditor BECAUSE "did not give notice in writing to the audited person that he had resigned by reason of his becoming ineligible"
    )
    LEST BREACH BY Auditor BECAUSE "did not resign his office immediately when the suspension notice took effect"

-- src:17504 | (3) A suspension notice does not make an Auditor General ineligible for appointment as a statutory auditor for the purposes of section 1213 (effect of ineligibility: criminal offences).
@ref s 1235(3) A suspension notice does not make the Auditor General ineligible for section 1213 (src:17504)
GIVEN `a suspension notice has effect in relation to the Auditor General` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1235(3) the suspension notice makes the Auditor General ineligible for the purposes of section 1213` MEANS
    IF `a suspension notice has effect in relation to the Auditor General`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A suspension notice does not make an Auditor General ineligible for appointment as a statutory auditor for the purposes of section 1213"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence speaks only of a suspension notice

§§§ `s 1236 Compliance orders`

-- src:17506 | (1) If at any time it appears to the Independent Supervisor that an Auditor General has failed to comply with an obligation imposed on him by or by virtue of this Part, the Independent Supervisor may make an application to the court under this section.
@ref s 1236(1) The Independent Supervisor may apply to the court (src:17506)
GIVEN `it appears to the Independent Supervisor that an Auditor General has failed to comply with an obligation imposed on him by or by virtue of Part 42` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1236(1) the Independent Supervisor may make an application to the court` MEANS
    IF `it appears to the Independent Supervisor that an Auditor General has failed to comply with an obligation imposed on him by or by virtue of Part 42`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If at any time it appears to the Independent Supervisor that an Auditor General has failed to comply with an obligation imposed on him by or by virtue of this Part, the Independent Supervisor may make an application": a grant limited by its own "if", so the case outside the limit is not decided here (name-test sweep of 2026-11-12, F26)

-- src:17507 | (2) If on an application under this section the court decides that the Auditor General has failed to comply with the obligation in question, it may order the Auditor General to take such steps as the court directs for securing that the obligation is complied with.
@ref s 1236(2) The court's order (src:17507)
GIVEN `an application is made under section 1236` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court decides that the Auditor General has failed to comply with the obligation in question` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1236(2) the court may order the Auditor General to take such steps as the court directs` MEANS
    IF `an application is made under section 1236` AND `the court decides that the Auditor General has failed to comply with the obligation in question`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If on an application under this section the court decides that the Auditor General has failed to comply with the obligation in question, it may order" (a failed "if", a lawyer's reading)

DECLARE `s 1236(3) court` IS ONE OF
    `s 1236(3) the High Court`
    `s 1236(3) the Court of Session`

-- src:17508 | (3) In this section “the court” means the High Court or, in Scotland, the Court of Session.
@ref s 1236(3) "the court" (src:17508)
GIVEN `the proceedings are in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 1236(3) court`
`s 1236(3) the court is` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are in Scotland`
    THEN `s 1236(3) the Court of Session`
    ELSE `s 1236(3) the High Court`

§§ `Proceedings`

§§§ `s 1237 Proceedings involving the Independent Supervisor`

-- src:17512 | (2) For this purpose “relevant proceedings” means proceedings brought in or in connection with the exercise of any function by the body as the Independent Supervisor.
