      `the proceedings are brought in the name of a body corporate whose constitution provides for the establishment of the body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1237(1) the proceedings may be brought by or against the Independent Supervisor in that name` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Independent Supervisor is an unincorporated association`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the Independent Supervisor is an unincorporated association"
    ELSE IF `coa26 support the answer is JUST TRUE` `the proceedings are relevant proceedings` AND `the proceedings are brought in the name of a body corporate whose constitution provides for the establishment of the body`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any relevant proceedings may be brought by or against it in the name of any body corporate whose constitution provides for the establishment of the body"

